<title>USA: Computer makers muscling into Hollywood market.</title>
<headline>Computer makers muscling into Hollywood market.</headline>
<byline>Sue Zeidler</byline>
<dateline>VENICE BEACH, Calif 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workstations made by Silicon Graphics Inc -- long a staple of the Hollywood special effects industry -- are facing sharp competition as other computer eye the lucrative market.</p>
<p>&quot;SGI is our pre-eminent platform. But I'm not wedded to any firm,&quot; said Scott Ross, chief executive of Digital Domain, an Oscar-nominated special effects company partly-owned by International Business Machines Corp. &quot;I'm wedded to performance and price. If you can show me something that performs better and costs less, I'll say SGI who?&quot;</p>
</text>
